# AI Academic Platform Database Schema

This document outlines the core entity relationships within the `academic_platform` database. 

## Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
    %% Core Organization
    DEPARTMENT {
        int id PK
        string name
        string code
    }
    REGULATION {
        int id PK
        string name
        int year
    }
    SEMESTER {
        int id PK
        string name
        int regulation_id FK
    }
    
    %% Users
    STUDENT {
        int id PK
        string full_name
        string register_number
        string college_email
        int department_id FK
        int regulation_id FK
        int current_semester FK
    }
    ADMIN_USER {
        int id PK
        string full_name
        string email
        string role "admin/staff"
        string department
    }
    
    %% Academics
    COURSE {
        int id PK
        string title
        string code
        int semester_id FK
    }
    UNIT {
        int id PK
        string title
        int course_id FK
    }
    TOPIC {
        int id PK
        string title
        int unit_id FK
    }
    
    %% Assessments
    TEST {
        int id PK
        string title
        string test_type
        int course_id FK
    }
    QUESTION {
        int id PK
        string question_text
        int test_id FK
        int topic_id FK
    }
    TEST_ATTEMPT {
        int id PK
        int test_id FK
        int student_id FK
    }
    TEST_RESULT {
        int id PK
        int attempt_id FK
        float score
        float percentage
    }
    
    %% Assignments & Tracking
    ASSIGNMENT {
        int id PK
        string title
        int course_id FK
    }
    ASSIGNMENT_SUBMISSION {
        int id PK
        int assignment_id FK
        int student_id FK
        float score
        string status
    }
    ATTENDANCE {
        int id PK
        int student_id FK
        date date
        string status
    }

    %% Relationships
    DEPARTMENT ||--o{ STUDENT : "has"
    REGULATION ||--o{ SEMESTER : "contains"
    REGULATION ||--o{ STUDENT : "follows"
    SEMESTER ||--o{ COURSE : "offers"
    SEMESTER ||--o{ STUDENT : "enrolled in"
    
    COURSE ||--o{ UNIT : "contains"
    COURSE ||--o{ TEST : "has"
    COURSE ||--o{ ASSIGNMENT : "has"
    
    UNIT ||--o{ TOPIC : "contains"
    
    TEST ||--o{ QUESTION : "contains"
    TEST ||--o{ TEST_ATTEMPT : "attempted via"
    
    STUDENT ||--o{ TEST_ATTEMPT : "takes"
    STUDENT ||--o{ ASSIGNMENT_SUBMISSION : "submits"
    STUDENT ||--o{ ATTENDANCE : "marked for"
    
    TEST_ATTEMPT ||--o| TEST_RESULT : "yields"
    ASSIGNMENT ||--o{ ASSIGNMENT_SUBMISSION : "receives"
```

## Key Modules
1. **Users & Org:** `students`, `admin_users` (staff/admins), `departments`, `regulations`, `semesters`.
2. **Curriculum:** `courses`, `units`, `topics`, `documents` (PDFs/RAG materials).
3. **Evaluation:** `tests`, `questions`, `test_attempts`, `test_results`, `test_answer_logs`.
4. **Assignments:** `assignments`, `assignment_submissions`.
5. **Tracking:** `attendance`, `student_progress`, `chat_history`.
